<title>GERMANY: Goldschmidt - 96 net profit down 52 pct.</title>
<headline>Goldschmidt - 96 net profit down 52 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996 (in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   11.8    vs 24.7</p>
<p>    Group sales				  1,413   vs 1,361</p>
<p>    Group operating profit		   32.6    vs 18.9</p>
<p>    Group pretax profit			36.1    vs 29.3</p>
<p>    Group investments			  112     vs 122</p>
<p>    Research and development costs	 66	vs 66</p>
<p>    Workforce (average)			6,029   vs 6,074</p>
<p>    Parent net profit			  25.5    vs 24.4</p>
<p>    Parent pre-tax profit		    42.8    vs 28.8</p>
<p>    Dividend (proposed)			12.0    vs 12.0 marks</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German chemicals company is Th. Goldschmidt AG. The group said that considerably higher tax payments as well as losses at foreign subsidiaries helped decrease net profit.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +4969 756525</p>
</text>
